<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="num-integers-operations">
  <title>Operations with Integers</title>

  <objectives>
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <ul>
      <li><xref ref="lo-n-7" /> — Operations with integers</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-n-6" /> — Properties of arithmetic</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <p>
    Adding a negative number is the same as subtracting a positive: <m>5 + (-3) = 5 - 3 = 2</m>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Subtracting a negative number is the same as adding: <m>5 - (-3) = 5 + 3 = 8</m>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For multiplication and division, the sign rules are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>positive × positive = positive: <m>3 \times 4 = 12</m></li>
    <li>negative × negative = positive: <m>(-3) \times (-4) = 12</m></li>
    <li>positive × negative = negative: <m>3 \times (-4) = -12</m></li>
    <li>negative × positive = negative: <m>(-3) \times 4 = -12</m></li>
  </ul>

  <exercises xml:id="exs-integers-ops">
    <title>Exercises</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-int-add">
      <statement><p>Calculate: <m>-8 + 3</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>-5</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p>Starting at <m>-8</m>, move 3 steps right: <m>-8 + 3 = -5</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-int-subtract-neg">
      <statement><p>Calculate: <m>4 - (-6)</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>4 - (-6) = 4 + 6 = 10</m></p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-int-multiply">
      <statement><p>Calculate: <m>(-5) \times (-3)</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>15</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p>Negative times negative gives positive: <m>(-5) \times (-3) = 15</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-int-divide">
      <statement><p>Calculate: <m>-24 \div 6</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>-4</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p>Negative divided by positive gives negative: <m>-24 \div 6 = -4</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

  </exercises>

</section>
